# Not used by the image build: the build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT
# (`docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .`), because the backend depends on
# rust/wasm-programs/pkg by path, and Docker reads the .dockerignore at the
# root of the context. The root .dockerignore must let these paths through:
#
#   backend  rust/Cargo.toml  rust/crates  rust/wasm-programs/pkg
#
# and should keep out **/target, **/.env and SQLite files. This file only
# matters if someone builds with backend/ as the context, which cannot work.
target
.env
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
